{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "reviewMethod": "Provisional assistant visual review via local OpenCV RGB contact sheets opened with view_image. First: 60 numerically ID-spread unreviewed nv_b_01.rar clips, five timestamped frames each on ten overview sheets. Then: 36 selected clips, 32 ordered source-frame samples spanning each complete clip. Finally: all consecutive source frames from frame zero through the first frame at or after 4.0 s for 18 candidate normal intervals (17 retained; nv_b_149 rejected after boundary inspection), visually inspected on timestamped full-frame contact sheets. cv2.setNumThreads(1); one sequential decoder; no GPU, audio or motion playback. Source seconds use decoded frame index / reported FPS. Evidence paths are repository-relative.",
  "limitations": [
    "Assistant screening labels are provisional training selections, not human ground truth. Publisher category was used only to find the archive pool, never as label approval.",
    "Only retained 0-4 s normal intervals have every-frame contact-sheet coverage. Full-clip 32-frame sheets and overview sheets are sampled; brief events between those samples may be missed. No continuous motion playback was performed.",
    "Contact sheets contain downscaled, blurred-face RGB thumbnails. Occlusion, distance, backlighting and absent audio limit judgments about contact mechanics. Every-frame inspection does not eliminate visual interpretation error.",
    "No identity, intent, injury, crime or relationship is inferred. Gesture-only and unclear contact scenes do not receive positive labels. Sports/prop scenes are excluded.",
    "sceneGroup describes visible backgrounds only; actors, sessions and source-media lineage are unknown. All records remain in the single VID training cohort, not independent calibration or holdout data.",
    "All tails after the retained four-second spans remain unannotated, including visually sampled tails that may appear normal.",
    "Selection intentionally favors campus settings, groups and movement; this is not a representative prevalence sample. No training or detector-performance claim follows from this review."
  ],
